<article class="env-remark" id="0EJ0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EJ0">Remark <span data-tag="0EJ0">52.18.3</span>.</a> Let $Y$ be a catenary Noetherian scheme and let $Z \subset Y$ be a closed subset. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0EIY" data-tag="0EIY">52.18.1</a> we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \delta _ Z(y) \leq \min \left\{  k \middle | \begin{matrix}  \text{ there exist specializations in }Y 

\\  y_0 \leftarrow y'_0 \rightarrow y_1 \leftarrow y'_1 \rightarrow \ldots \leftarrow y'_{k - 1} \rightarrow y_ k = y 

\\  \text{ with }y_0 \in Z\text{ and }y_ i' \leadsto y_ i \text{ immediate} 

\end{matrix} \right\}   \]
</div>
  <p> We claim that if $Y$ is of finite type over a field, then equality holds. If we ever need this result we will formulate a precise result and prove it here. However, in general if we define $\delta _ Z$ by the right hand side of this inequality, then we don't know if Lemma <a href="/tag/0EIZ" data-tag="0EIZ">52.18.2</a> remains true. </p>
</article>